{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/485713-north-korea-s-supernatural-phenomenon-classic-edition","id":485713,"title":"North Korea's Supernatural Phenomenon, Classic Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-19T14:25:27-07:00","id":485713,"title":"North Korea's Supernatural Phenomenon, Classic Edition","content":"Because I just realized the country doesn't need to be darkened at all to be Gothic Punk instead of Modern Gothic.<br /> <br /> A clone of my other thread, what say the cWoD's fans about the kind of supernatural stuff that sprouts up in the Hermit Kingdom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T00:00:19-07:00","id":486059,"title":"","content":"Well my Google Fu found this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korean_mythology\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/05/Mansindo_%28%E8%90%AC%E7%A5%9E%E5%9C%96%29%2C_early_19th-c._Korean_shamanic_painting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korean_mythology\" target=\"_blank\"> Korean mythology - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korean_mythology\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korean_mythology </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T02:01:59-07:00","id":486149,"title":"","content":"Would Northeren Korean mythology be drastically different then Southern Korean mythology? Their separation is largely artificial, and the communist regime would not condone any religious or mythic influences resurging there so there surely are no new developments beyond those Shen who simply are there already?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T06:35:15-07:00","id":486282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/485713-north-korea-s-supernatural-phenomenon-classic-edition?p=486149#post486149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Northeren Korean mythology be drastically different then Southern Korean mythology? Their separation is largely artificial, and the communist regime would not condone any religious or mythic influences resurging there so there surely are no new developments beyond those Shen who simply are there already?</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt there are any major differences in the core myth, but I also don't doubt there's some major differences in the real Shen; I can't help but wonder if the nicest faction there are Devil-Tigers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T18:01:40-07:00","id":487822,"title":"","content":"I am not much of an expert on the cWoD, but the werefoxes (I think they are just called kitsune in cWoD) in korea (also known as Gumiho) are cannibals in the myths. North Korea is where the foxes fallen to the Wyrm gather to discuss their plans and brag about the tricks they have pulled on the servants of Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T22:29:05-07:00","id":487987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/485713-north-korea-s-supernatural-phenomenon-classic-edition?p=486282#post486282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt there are any major differences in the core myth, but I also don't doubt there's some major differences in the real Shen; I can't help but wonder if the nicest faction there are Devil-Tigers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Koreas are austenibly under the Green Courts which are known for their mecenary and necromantic focuses(SO lots of boneflowers). The Crane book says something about North Korea being a failed experiment by one of their Wu.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/485713-north-korea-s-supernatural-phenomenon-classic-edition?p=487822#post487822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not much of an expert on the cWoD, but the werefoxes (I think they are just called kitsune in cWoD) in korea (also known as Gumiho) are cannibals in the myths. North Korea is where the foxes fallen to the Wyrm gather to discuss their plans and brag about the tricks they have pulled on the servants of Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Fox spirits aren't exactly super nice in Japanese and chinese legends either, while I can see using Gumiho for Fallen Kitsune, it might be better to spread them out rather than &quot;North Korea is all wyrm all the time&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T01:10:42-07:00","id":528633,"title":"","content":"Well, given that the Korean kuei-jin run a brisk trade in smuggling supernaturals into/out of China (for a price), almost anything could be run into on the &quot;Parallel Path&quot;. Well, anything that can afford to pay their (rather steep) fee.<br /> <br /> And there should be a plethora of Chinese wraiths, too. Like most of the Asian Shadowlands, the Korean portion of the Underworld is under the &quot;benevolent administration&quot; of the Dark Kingdom of Jade (i.e. Chinese wraiths invaded and conquered their Korean neighbors).<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Nagaraja bloodline of Cainites has recently (as of 2000) sought refuge in the Koreas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/485713-north-korea-s-supernatural-phenomenon-classic-edition?p=487987#post487987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both Koreas are austenibly under the Green Courts which are known for their mecenary and necromantic focuses(SO lots of boneflowers). The Crane book says something about North Korea being a failed experiment by one of their Wu. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Koreas were. The Resplendant Crane dharma decided to take advantage of the partitioning of the Korean peninsula, to experiment with different styles of governing. And, in the eyes of the Cranes, both are horrific failures. North Korea was <i>supposed</i> to be a shining example of the virtues of totalitarianism - not an impoverished basket case.<br /> <br /> But that failure is bringing even <i>more</i> supernaturals to the Korean Peninsula . Many of the disappointed Cranes (in typical kuei-jin fashion) are rallying around the theory that their Korean experiments failed because of the human residents - humans aren't &quot;good&quot; enough to be &quot;properly&quot; ruled. To that end, they're trying to breed &quot;better&quot; humans. So there could be all sorts of experimental fomori and bizarre mutant humans running around, too.<br /> <br /> Even worse, these disaffected Cranes are starting to flirt with Infernalism (even outright demonic pacts). Many demonic investments are just so <i>helpful</i>, in their experimental breeding program. . . And, of course, the kuei-jin are <i>sure</i> they're the ones in control . . . So the Koreas should have more than their fair share of demons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 06-06-2015, 04:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T06:11:57-07:00","id":528741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/485713-north-korea-s-supernatural-phenomenon-classic-edition?p=487987#post487987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both Koreas are austenibly under the Green Courts which are known for their mecenary and necromantic focuses(SO lots of boneflowers).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think any of my groups will ever end up in NK, but the Green Court/necromancy angle makes me think of the alleged status of NK in WWZ...basically, if you haven't read it, the entire population apparently retreated into the miles of tunnels and bunkers under the country to wait the zombie apocalypse out, but no one's made contact with them in years. The rest of the world isn't willing to risk the attempt, because there's a creeping suspicion that the millions of Koreans that went underground are now all zombies, shuffling around and waiting for some nice person to let them out.<br /> <br /> Obviously too over-the-top for the WoD, at least on a large scale, but on a smaller scale...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}